course: dictionary
lesson: 129
title: Adventurous: brave and curious
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adventurous means liking to try new, exciting things, even when they might be a little risky. It is an adjective, so it describes a person, a place or a thing, and it can change: adventurous, more adventurous, most adventurous.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. «Portly is Otter's little son; he often strays and turns up again, because, says the Mole, «he's so adventurous».» Portly wanders off and comes back, so adventurous must mean that he likes to explore. Swap in brave and curious: «he's so brave and curious» still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe things, not just people. «An adventurous journey» is full of excitement and danger. «An adventurous menu» is new and bold, not the usual food. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Being adventurous is good, but think about danger first, and always tell an adult where you are going. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is too adventurous and gets into trouble, so being adventurous does not mean being careless.
fact: Adventurous means liking to try new, exciting and sometimes risky things.
fact: «Adventurous» can describe a person, such as «he's so adventurous», or a thing, such as «an adventurous journey».
fact: «Adventurous» is an adjective, and it changes to «more adventurous» and «most adventurous».
fact: In «an adventurous menu», the word means new and bold, not the usual.
fact: Being adventurous is good, but think about danger and tell an adult where you are going.
exercise: «Portly often strays and turns up again, because, says the Mole, «he's so adventurous».» What does adventurous mean here? | Very tired and sleepy | Angry with his family | Lost and never found again | * Brave and curious, liking to explore
exercise: In The Wind in the Willows, the shy Mole leaves his spring-cleaning and goes to the river. Which word best describes him then? | Noisy | Lazy | * Adventurous | Frightened of everything
exercise: What does «an adventurous journey» mean? | Done only in the dark | * Full of excitement and danger | Boring and long | Very short and slow
test: «Be adventurous – try a new food!» What does this mean? | Eat only sweets | Do not eat at all | * Be brave and try something new | Only eat the same food as always
test: What is the safest way to be adventurous? | Run off alone without telling anyone | * Think about danger first and tell an adult where you are going | Follow strangers who call to you | Climb the highest tree without asking
exam: Which word completes the list? adventurous, ___, most adventurous | adventurous more | * more adventurous | adventureful | adventury
